<title>USA: UPS, Teamsters resume talks amid optimism.</title>
<headline>UPS, Teamsters resume talks amid optimism.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Negotiators for United Parcel Service and the Teamsters union resumed talks on Friday amid optimism they may be getting closer to a deal to end a 12-day strike against the nation's largest package carrier.</p>
<p>Federal mediators met with UPS and union negotiators separately early on Friday, Federal Mediation and Conciliation Service spokesman David Helfert said. Mediators briefed Labor Secretary Alexis Herman on the status of the talks, which had recessed at about 1:45 a.m. EDT (0545 GMT).</p>
</text>
